    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0115" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 3A/4–847: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McGurk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-08T17:00:00-03:00">April 8, 1947—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>138. For Dreier from Boal. After talking with Carbajal, Góes,<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d90-f1"/> Peruvian and Venezuelan members, in general sense of that
                    part of your 105, April 3, [<hi rendition="#italic">2</hi>] dealing with scope
                    of CPD’s functions, Carbajal tells me he agrees
                    it is best to delay any suggestion for CPD
                    action <pb facs="0116" n="100" xml:id="pg100"/> in order to leave question open
                    for Government’s confidential examination at Rio or Bogotá. This matter was not
                    mentioned at today’s meeting. [Boal.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McGurk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d90-f1" n="16" xml:id="d90-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Pedro A. Góes Monteiro, Brazilian member on the Emergency Advisory Committee
                    for Political Defense.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
